{{ 'dev-faq.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'dev-faq.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Section: "FAQ" (dev name `faq`). Page: /pages/faq.

  THERE IS NO FAQ ARTBOARD. The Figma file has Homepage, Our Story, Tree-Fibre, Contact, Delivery,
  Shipping and PDP — and no FAQ. So this section is not pixel-verified against a reference the way
  its siblings were, and nobody should go looking for the mock that "must" exist.

  What it is instead: the accordion from `Accordions - Desktop` (45068:1975), the component already
  built into dev-main-product, reused so the page reads as part of the site. Its 944px width is the
  one measured value taken from Figma here.

  The rows are <details>/<summary>, not a div plus a click handler. They open with no JS, they are
  keyboard operable and announced correctly by screen readers for free, and Ctrl+F on the page can
  still find the text inside a closed panel. dev-faq.js only upgrades them.

  The ~40 lines of accordion JS are duplicated from dev-main-product rather than shared. The
  standard is three files per section; coupling two sections through a shared asset to save forty
  lines would cost more than the duplication does.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} Fixed design tokens — not merchant-controlled {%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .dev-faq {

    {%- comment -%} The width of the Accordions - Desktop artboard (45068:1975). A question is a line of prose:
       run it to the 1312px page container and it becomes a hard read. {%- endcomment -%}
    --container-max: 944px;
    --section-px: 64px;
    --section-px-mobile: 16px;

    --font-heading-size: 32px;
    --font-heading-size-mobile: 24px;
    {%- comment -%} Desktop/Title 4 — the same step the PDP's accordion headings sit on. {%- endcomment -%}
    --font-question-size: 22px;
    --font-heading-weight: 500;
    --font-heading-lh: 1.2;

    --font-answer-size: 18px;
    --font-answer-size-mobile: 16px;
    --font-body-lh: 1.4;
    --w-medium: 500;

    --head-gap: 40px;
    --icon-size: 24px;

    {%- comment -%} 24px on the artboard, in three places: under the divider, between question and answer, and
       between one row's answer and the next divider. {%- endcomment -%}
    --acc-gap: 24px;

    {%- comment -%} One curve for the accordion, both directions — opening on one curve and closing on another
       looks restless when a row closes while its neighbour opens. The JS reads --acc-dur back out
       of here (parseFloat on the computed value), so keep it in ms.

       DO NOT RETUNE THESE TO "MATCH DELIVERY & RETURNS". Checked against dev-policy.liquid on
       2026-08-17: it declares the same 300ms and the same cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1), and says
       in its own token comment that it took them FROM here. Both sections animate height with the
       same Web Animations call (dev-policy.js is dev-faq.js with the data-* hooks renamed), rotate
       the chevron on the same CSS transition, and fade the answer in over the same 0.75 x
       --acc-dur. The timing is already identical to the millisecond, so editing either value here
       would CREATE the difference it was meant to remove. What reads as a different speed is
       behaviour, not duration — see the long note in dev-faq.js. {%- endcomment -%}
    --acc-dur: 300ms;
    --acc-ease: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);

    {%- comment -%} Closing note ("Still got questions?"). Owner, 2026-08-17: they wanted the closing block from
       Delivery & Returns on the FAQ page. It is dev-policy's `note` block (45246:3617), carried
       over whole.

       These are RESTATED here rather than borrowed from the question tokens above, because
       dev-policy sizes the note off its own scale and it does not line up with this section's:
       the note's body is Body/Md 16px, while --font-answer-size here is Body/Lg 18px. Reusing the
       FAQ answer size would make it a slightly different component, which is the one thing this
       change is not allowed to do. The 22px heading equals --font-question-size by coincidence,
       not by reference — kept separate so a later change to the questions cannot drag the note
       with it. {%- endcomment -%}
    --note-pt: 24px;
    --note-gap: 8px;
    --font-note-size: 22px;
    --font-note-size-mobile: 20px;
    --font-note-body-size: 16px;
  }
</style>

<div
  class="dev-faq"
  style="
    --bg: {{ section.settings.background_color }};
    --color: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    --accent: {{ section.settings.accent_color }};
    --border-color: {{ section.settings.border_color }};
    --pt: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
    --pb: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
  "
  data-faq
>
  <div class="dev-faq__inner">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank or section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
      <div class="dev-faq__head">
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
          <h1>, not <h2>. This section IS the page's main content — the page templates render no
          title of their own, so before this the whole document had no h1 at all and its outline
          opened at level 2. The children below are h2 for the same reason: an h1 followed by an h3
          is a skipped level.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="dev-faq__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="dev-faq__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign questions = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
      assign notes = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'note'
    -%}
    {%- if questions.size > 0 or notes.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="dev-faq__list" data-faq-group{% if section.settings.single_open %} data-faq-single-open{% endif %}>
        {%- for block in questions -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Aug 2026 review fix. A Question row is only drawn once it HAS a question. Without this
            guard, the moment the owner clicks "Add Question" and saves before typing (or clears a
            heading), the <summary> renders with nothing in it but the aria-hidden chevron — a
            keyboard- and screen-reader-focusable disclosure control with no accessible name at all
            (WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value), announced as a nameless "collapsed" button. The block
            settings now carry defaults too, so the editor starts from real copy rather than blank,
            but defaults only cover the ADD; they do not stop a heading being emptied afterwards.
            Same guard dev-policy's question loop carries.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.heading == blank -%}
            {%- continue -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <details
            class="dev-faq__item"
            data-faq-item
            {% if block.settings.open_by_default %}open{% endif %}
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <summary class="dev-faq__summary">
              <h2 class="dev-faq__question">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h2>
              <span class="dev-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- comment -%} One glyph, rotated when the row opens — a second SVG would be the same path drawn twice. {%- endcomment -%}
                <svg class="dev-faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" focusable="false">
                  <path d="M19 9L12 16L5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>

            {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
              <div class="dev-faq__answer">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </details>
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The "Still got questions?" group, lifted from dev-policy (45246:3617) at the owner's ask,
          2026-08-17 — the closing block from Delivery & Returns, on the FAQ page.

          Same construction as there, deliberately: it sits INSIDE the list so it picks up the
          list's 24px flex gap and then adds its own 24px pad on top, landing 48px clear of the
          last question — the same 24 + 24 dev-policy gets from --qa-gap plus --note-pt.

          It is NOT a .dev-faq__item. That class carries the row rules and the accordion padding,
          and the note is neither a row nor collapsible. It also carries no [data-faq-item], so
          dev-faq.js walks straight past it, and it is not in `questions`, so it can never leak
          into the FAQPage ld+json below as a fake Q&A pair.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for block in notes -%}
          <div class="dev-faq__note" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
              <h2 class="dev-faq__note-heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h2>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
              <div class="dev-faq__note-body">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  schema.org/FAQPage, built from the same blocks the section renders — so the structured data cannot
  drift from what is on the page. `strip_html` on the answer because the spec wants text, not markup;
  `json` on both because a merchant's apostrophe would otherwise break the document.

  Aug 2026 review fix — only blocks with BOTH a question and an answer enter the graph. Google
  rejects an FAQPage whose entries carry an empty `name` or an empty answer `text`, and one bad
  entry can invalidate the whole block for /pages/faq, which is the only page carrying this
  section. A half-filled row is exactly what the theme editor produces between "Add Question" and
  the owner typing, so the loop cannot assume every block is complete. The tags are stripped and
  &nbsp; folded to a space BEFORE the test for the reason the policy card body does it: the
  richtext editor leaves "<p>&nbsp;</p>" behind when you clear a line, which is not blank to Liquid
  but is blank to a reader — and to Google.

  The count is taken in a first pass because the comma between entries can no longer come from
  `forloop.last`: the last BLOCK may well be one of the skipped ones. `printed` counts what has
  actually been emitted and the comma is written before each entry after the first.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign faq_entries = 0
  for block in questions
    assign q_name = block.settings.heading | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip
    assign q_text = block.settings.body | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip
    if q_name != blank and q_text != blank
      assign faq_entries = faq_entries | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if faq_entries > 0 -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {%- assign printed = 0 -%}
        {%- for block in questions -%}
          {%- assign q_name = block.settings.heading | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip -%}
          {%- assign q_text = block.settings.body | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip -%}
          {%- if q_name != blank and q_text != blank -%}
            {%- if printed > 0 %},{% endif -%}
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": {{ q_name | json }},
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": {{ q_text | strip_newlines | json }}
              }
            }
            {%- assign printed = printed | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Frequently Asked Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subheading"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "single_open",
      "label": "Close other rows when one opens",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off, every row stays open until you close it, so two answers can be compared side by side. On, opening a row closes whichever was open. Off matches the FAQ page."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Background",
      "info": "Transparent by default — the section inherits the page canvas.",
      "default": "rgba(0,0,0,0)"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text color",
      "default": "#333333"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent",
      "default": "#4EA448"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "Divider",
      "default": "#C4BCA9"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding top",
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding bottom",
      "default": 80
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "inline_richtext",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "How are trees turned into duvets?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>The wood is broken down into pulp, spun into soft fibres and then used to fill our duvets.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "open_by_default",
          "label": "Open by default",
          "default": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "name": "Closing note",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "inline_richtext",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Still got questions?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "<p><a href=\"/pages/contact\">Click here</a> to chat with us</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How soon will my order arrive?",
            "body": "<p>UK orders are dispatched within one working day and usually arrive in two to three.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How much does delivery cost?",
            "body": "<p>Standard delivery is free to all UK addresses.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "note"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
